@* The trigger is `absolute inset-0`: an invisible sheet over the whole card, not a wrapper
   around it. Nest the media and the text inside and they position absolutely too and escape the
   card. Its own content should be a name and nothing else, because a link with no text is
   announced as its own URL.

   Two forms, and both have to actually do something. The link opens the file in a tab —
   target="_blank" as shadcn's own example does, so the thread you were reading stays where it
   was. The button posts, because a button outside a form with no handler is inert, and inert is
   indistinguishable from broken. *@
<div class="flex w-[320px] flex-col gap-3">
    <Attachment>
        <AttachmentMedia><Icon Name="file" /></AttachmentMedia>
        <AttachmentContent>
            <AttachmentTitle>acme-msa.pdf</AttachmentTitle>
            <AttachmentDescription>Opens in a tab</AttachmentDescription>
        </AttachmentContent>
        <AttachmentTrigger Href="/files/acme-msa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            <span class="sr-only">Open acme-msa.pdf</span>
        </AttachmentTrigger>
    </Attachment>

    <form method="post" action="/files/draft.md/preview" up-target=".preview" up-disable>
        <AntiforgeryToken />
        <Attachment>
            <AttachmentMedia><Icon Name="file" /></AttachmentMedia>
            <AttachmentContent>
                <AttachmentTitle>draft.md</AttachmentTitle>
                <AttachmentDescription>A button, for something that is not a URL</AttachmentDescription>
            </AttachmentContent>
            <AttachmentTrigger name="file" value="draft.md">
                <span class="sr-only">Preview draft.md</span>
            </AttachmentTrigger>
        </Attachment>
    </form>
</div>
